OK, but there were issues!
Tests: 4, Assertions: 13, PHPUnit Deprecations: 1.

Tests covering AC1:
- test_two_racers_holding_the_same_stale_token_produce_exactly_one_remint:
  simulates 2 racers sharing the same stale token via sequential calls to
  remintOauthTokenOnUnauthorized() against the same cache key. Winner forgets
  + remints (Http::assertSentCount goes 1->2); loser (same stale token,
  arriving after) reuses the winner's already-reminted token via the
  double-checked cache read — Http::assertSentCount stays at 2 (never 3).
  This is exactly AC1: "exactly ONE Cache::forget + ONE OAuth remint reaches
  Google (not two independent mints)".
- test_lock_contention_timeout_fails_closed_returns_null_no_exception:
  confirms Cache::lock(...)->block(5,...) timeout fails closed (returns null,
  no resend, no bubbled exception) when another holder has the lock.
- test_send_notification_to_http_401_path_still_reminted_and_retried_end_to_end:
  confirms the full sendNotificationToHttp() 401->remint->retry path still
  resolves correctly through the new lock wrapper.

Backend log corroboration (Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log, testing channel,
