Caveat (stated explicitly per engineer's note and QA's own read of the test):
these tests exercise the double-check/lock logic SEQUENTIALLY in a single
PHP process (Laravel Cache::lock backed by phpunit's forced CACHE_DRIVER=array,
which is an in-process store) — this proves the LOGIC ORDERING (double-checked
cache read inside the lock) is correct, not true multi-process concurrency
against a shared cache backend (redis/database in production). No live/manual
concurrent-request demonstration was possible for this AC (no UI trigger, and
genuine multi-process racing isn't practical to stage in a QA pass) — this is
disclosed, not silently assumed away.
